From b83b8039bd1a7b8efdf249dc2cc6a5119d425e0f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nishith Khanna <nishith.khanna@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 14:55:20 +0530
Subject: TEMP: bundle eyeo's partner anti-circumvention list

Not for shipping. This makes YouTube ad blocking testable without
depending on a filter list server we do not have yet.

The public abp-filters-anti-cv.txt carries ~300 snippet filters and none
of them target YouTube. Those live in a separate set of per-product
overlays in eyeo's anti-cv repository, under distribution/:

  abp-filters-core.txt      "Filters to be used by core products"
  abp-filters-AB.txt        "Filters to be used by Adblock"
  abp-filters-partners.txt  "Filters to be used by distribution partners"

We are a browser vendor shipping the SDK, so partners is the one that
applies to us. It is also what Cromite's experimental-cromite-filters.txt
was derived from, except that copy is a stale 20-line snapshot while
upstream is 72 lines and maintained.

Uses the mechanism eyeo documents in docs/integration-how-to.md:

 - abp_filters_partners.txt.gz added next to the other bundled lists
 - make_abp_partners converts it to a flatbuffer at build time
 - IDR_ADBLOCK_FLATBUFFER_ABP_PARTNERS packs it into the pak
 - GetPreloadedSubscriptionConfiguration() serves it while the list is
   subscribed but not yet downloaded, so blocking works on first launch
   with no network at all
 - subscribed at first run with AllowedAndChecked, which is what eyeo
   documents as the requirement for snippet filters to load

kAllowPrivilegedFilters now defaults to true. This is not optional here:
converter_main.cc converts bundled lists with allow_privileged=true, so
the bundled copy keeps its snippets either way, but the preloaded copy
is dropped as soon as the real list downloads. With the pref off, that
downloaded copy has its snippets stripped by FlatbufferSerializer and
YouTube ads would return after the first successful update.

18 of the 23 snippet rules survive Cromite's kAllowedSnippets allowlist.
The 5 that do not use simulate-mouse-event (which uazo marked
"unsupported", consistent with him removing trusted events), plus
event-override and map-override, which the bundled snippet library 2.15.0
does not implement either. Those are the rules that click the Skip Ad
button; the json-prune and override-property-read rules that strip ad
placements out of the player response are unaffected.

Before shipping: mirror this on an e Foundation host rather than
fetching from gitlab.com, and confirm we are entitled to redistribute a
list eyeo labels for distribution partners.
